  "title": "Mutiny on the Bounty",
  "summary": "On 28 April 1789, near Tofua in Tonga, Fletcher Christian and about twenty-five men seized the Bounty and set Captain William Bligh and 18 loyalists adrift in a 23-foot launch. Bligh reached Kupang, Timor, on 14 June after 48 days; Christian's group later settled on Pitcairn Island in January 1790.",
